# Dirtree: Stateful directory trees in the CLI for humans and LLMs. https://github.com/pmarreck/dirtree
ver=1.2
annotate=[
	ADR.tsv = Fleet decision log (TSV, printable-binary encoded fields); adr-0001 documents its own format
	INTENT.md = Purpose and verification boundaries of the shared skills repository
	MECHATRON_PRIME_CI.md = Portable Mechatron Prime CI target, webhook, and badge policy.
	PLAN.md = Active and recently completed work for the shared cross-agent skill repository.
	about-peter = Directory symlink to the private about-peter skill whose SKILL.md remains outside this public repo.
	capture-collaboration-evidence = Proactively identifies and records artifact-backed cases where human-agent synthesis beats either starting approach.
	cross-platform-project-build-arch = Cross-agent target output, PATH publication, and bundle build convention
	cross-platform-project-build-arch/SKILL.md = Approved platform-specific entrypoints and shared build command contract
	cross-platform-project-build-arch/references/canonical-implementations.md = Canonical implementation selection, unified build scope, optional ABI variants and migration tests
	cross-platform-project-build-arch/references/verification-and-migration.md = Acceptance scenarios and scoped rollout checklist for build/PATH migration
	deep-code-review = Audit a codebase or major subsystem for quality and missed issues at project milestones.
	deep-code-review/SKILL.md = Cross-agent contract-led code review with verified findings, explicit coverage and optional bounded delegation
	deep-code-review/references/review-lenses.md = Conditional review lenses for tests, recovery, complexity, security, ownership, FFI and operational contracts
	dispatch = Dispatch background subagents for substantial tasks, fanning out parallel work with progress checkpointing.
	docs/PLAN_LOG.md = Completed plan items and historical verification evidence
	docs/plan_context/follow-ups.md = Deferred implementation scope and inbox reconciliation evidence
	erect-agent-stack = Stand up or join a project's agent stack — tmux session + remoted coding agent — in one idempotent command.
	erect-agent-stack/SKILL.md = Herdr project-agent discovery, persistent context, launch and reuse workflow
	fix-zig-deps-hash = Fix nix build zigDeps/zigDepsHash mismatches after build.zig.zon dependency changes.
	flake.nix = Pure Nix test environment declaring Bash, LuaJIT, and every suite tool and patched script interpreter.
	gather-project-intentions = Cross-agent project intent discovery, safe overview migration, and focused owner interviews
	handoff = Condense current dev state into a handoff doc conveying purpose and intent to the next agent.
	i18n = Canonical i18n discipline: 50-locale set, compile-time enforcement, bilingual errors, RTL, --lang/--help conventions.
	i18n/SKILL.md = Canonical opt-in i18n discipline: scope decision gate, 50 locales, enforcement, bilingual errors, RTL, and localized CLI conventions.
	install = Cross-platform installer linking one physical skill repo into Claude and Codex with recoverable legacy migration.
	llmsend = Inter-session/inter-machine LLMsend messaging skill (symlink into the ../llmsend project).
	llvm-guided-optimization = Optimize Zig hot paths via hand-tuned LLVM IR when algorithmic gains are exhausted.
	mechatron-ci = Shared Mechatron Prime CI skill with Codex UI metadata.
	memories = Shared cross-agent workflow for typed durable memory recall, migration, validation, and consolidation.
	memories/SKILL.md = Generic public contract for durable shared/project memory recall, UTC metadata, migration, validation, and consolidation.
	memories/scripts/check-frontmatter = Validates memory YAML headers while pruning VCS metadata and generated .codescan search indexes.
	memories/scripts/list-titles = Lists shared and project memory titles or validated headers; sourceable as list_memory_titles.
	memories/scripts/migrate-legacy = Previews or safely migrates legacy memories, preserving bodies and rendering creation instants as UTC.
	mfic = Design/judge tests and gates for trustworthiness — Mechanically-Falsifiable Independent Controls for LLM-produced work.
	onboard/SKILL.md = onboard skill: rebuild a dead session's context from its on-disk transcript (converse of handoff)
	onboard/scripts/collect-claude-context = Bash: day-anchored session selection for a cwd, reduces and concatenates for a summarising subagent
	onboard/scripts/reduce-claude-transcript = LuaJIT: reduce one Claude session .jsonl to Markdown ~18x smaller; whitelisted record types, unknown = hard error
	performance-profiling = Cross-agent runtime, complexity, memory and external-history benchmark contract
	planning-work = PLAN.md discipline: one-line checkboxes, retirement to docs/PLAN_LOG.md, context in docs/plan_context/
	planning-work/scripts = LuaJIT plan-unwrap, plan-retire and plan-lint sharing the plan_lib.lua line classifier
	scaffold-zig-project = Scaffold a new greenfield Zig project from scratch.
	ship = Commit and push known-green work, watch Mechatron Prime CI, or cut a tagged GitHub release.
	test = Runs the complete llm_skills installer and skill-policy regression suite.
	test-isolation = Test-owned state and preventive filesystem boundaries
	test-isolation/scripts/run-isolated = Linux read-only host view with private test HOME and scratch
	tests/cli/test_i18n_scope_policy = Regression guard for the i18n skill's explicit owner-decision and RULES.md recording gate.
	tests/cli/test_install = Regression tests for installer options, canonical skill-root links, shared metadata, and rerun safety.
	tests/cli/test_memories = Regression-tests frontmatter validation, legacy migration, repository scaffolding, and .codescan pruning.
	tests/cli/test_memory_titles = Classifies shared/project memory discovery and proves headers ignore VCS and .codescan metadata.
	tests/cli/test_onboard_collect = tests day-anchored selection: whole newest day, size-floor walk-back, calendar bound, --list/--session
	tests/cli/test_onboard_reducer = classifier-over-sets tests for the reducer: sensitivity, specificity, payload bound, reduction ratio, drift failure
	tests/cli/test_planning_work = Classifier-over-sets, unwrap, lint and retire behavior tests for the planning-work scripts
	tests/cli/test_retired_garnix_guidance = Regression gate preventing shared workflows from resurrecting retired Garnix CI guidance.
	tests/cli/test_writing_nix_skill = Integration contract for skill discovery, Git input classification, source attribution, and ecosystem comparison.
	tests/cli/test_zero_copy_install = Integration test for zero-copy Codex skill installation, safe legacy archival, idempotence, and hook retirement.
	universal-app-frontend/SKILL.md = Cross-agent desktop frontend stack and GPUI dependency selection guidance
	universal-app-frontend/agents/openai.yaml = Codex discovery metadata for the shared frontend skill
	universal-app-frontend/references/application-pattern.md = Dated application manifest evidence, dependency pins and platform pitfalls
	walking-decisions = Shared skill for narration-first owner decisions and fixed answer routing
	writing-bend/SKILL.md = Bend 2 toolchain, pure-core, proof and backend workflow with task-specific reference routing
	writing-bend/examples/LAWS.bend = Separate length, carry endpoint and empty-fold propositions over the real model
	writing-bend/examples/Library.bend = Single compiled JS facade for constructing and consuming the example model coherently
	writing-bend/examples/Model.bend = Pure U32-limb carry, little-endian encoding and structurally recursive fold examples
	writing-bend/examples/PROOF.bend = Proof terms checked against the imported executable model laws
	writing-bend/examples/check-sdk.mjs = Independent JS assertions for emitted codec content, limb carry/wrap and fold results
	writing-bend/examples/main.bend = Tiny native I/O edge printing the pure model's carry and fold results
	writing-bend/references/interop.md = Pure effect interpretation, coherent JS facades, native C runtime embedding and separate SDK artifacts
	writing-bend/references/language.md = Verified Bend 2 syntax, affine callbacks, structural termination and exact limb arithmetic traps
	writing-bend/references/measurements.md = Measured performance/statistics lessons and Bend-oracle plus Zig-kernel refinement workflow
	writing-bend/references/proofs.md = Executable-linked laws, pinned verdict kernel, independent controls and proof trust boundaries
	writing-bend/references/sources.md = Pinned upstream documentation, reproducible example commands and bounded verification receipts
	writing-nix/SKILL.md = Routes Nix authoring, packaging, diagnosis, activation, and ecosystem-lore work through scoped references.
	writing-nix/agents/openai.yaml = Codex display metadata and default prompt for the writing-nix skill.
	writing-nix/references/derivations-and-packaging.md = Dependency roles, derivation phases, hooks, IFD, cross builds, and language dependency caching.
	writing-nix/references/diagnostics-and-activation.md = Layered Nix diagnosis, fixed-output failures, closure safety, and NixOS activation gates.
	writing-nix/references/ecosystem-and-community.md = Nix ecosystem lore, project tradeoffs, coexistence boundaries, governance history, and contribution policy.
	writing-nix/references/sources-and-flakes.md = Git source visibility, path-input behavior, source filtering, and flake-check contracts.
	writing-nix/scripts/check-flake-inputs = Read-only Git-index classifier for task-required inputs to Git-backed flakes.
	writing-roc = Compiler-aware Roc quick reference and validated examples for cross-agent use
	writing-roc/examples = Network-free syntax and imported-module smoke examples
	zig-microbenchmarks = Add benchmarks to a Zig project, track hot-path performance, and investigate regressions.
]
